1
00:00:00,666 --> 00:00:02,400
Welcome back boys

2
00:00:03,266 --> 00:00:07,733
Today we are going to finally start doing something related to Reika's mods

3
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:12,000
We have a lot of different books from which to choose where to start

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,766
and we are going to start with RotaryCraft

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,566
This is a mod based around gears and axles

6
00:00:18,566 --> 00:00:21,366
and the power is given by torque times speed

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,600
But, before we get started, we should probably secure an area around our base

8
00:00:28,166 --> 00:00:32,833
that is to keep us safe from creatures that exist only to make our game less fun

9
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:37,233
Next, to make our base look cooler and not get dirty

10
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:40,966
we shall replace the dirt with some nicer looking stone bricks

11
00:00:41,566 --> 00:00:45,200
Finally, we make a small farm to sustain ourselves

12
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,733
And now it is time to fill this land with machines

13
00:00:50,466 --> 00:00:54,600
The first machine we are going to try to run is an extractor

14
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,533
This is a machine which processes raw ores with a four-step operation

15
00:00:58,533 --> 00:01:02,266
which will quintuple the yield when compared to a vanilla furnace

16
00:01:02,533 --> 00:01:07,200
while also giving some extra by-products that can only be obtained that way

17
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,700
This machine has some particular power requirements

18
00:01:11,066 --> 00:01:13,966
so we are also going to need a power source

19
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:17,133
The most affordable one is probably steam engines

20
00:01:17,766 --> 00:01:21,933
These will require water, so we should probably start with a pump

21
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:26,233
which we will power with the weakest, redstone-powered generator

22
00:01:26,966 --> 00:01:30,300
We start by placing down the redstone motor

23
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,000
which will start spinning as soon as we give it a redstone signal

24
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:40,333
Using a screwdriver, we rotate it towards the water, where we can place a pump

25
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,500
However, as you can see, the pump is not working

26
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:50,333
The power requirement is 1 kilowatt, which is exactly the power our motor produces

27
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,000
but we are not providing enough torque

28
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,700
To fix that, we shall add a 4 to 1 ratio gearbox

29
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,000
which will trade speed for force

30
00:02:00,466 --> 00:02:02,666
However, that still doesn't work

31
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,700
The issue is that this gearbox is in speed mode

32
00:02:05,966 --> 00:02:10,433
once we turn it in torque mode, the pump starts filling up with water

33
00:02:11,166 --> 00:02:13,933
which we can finally move with a liquid pipe

34
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:18,200
Now we can use that water to feed 4 steam engines

35
00:02:19,033 --> 00:02:23,433
However, they don't run just on water, they also need some heat

36
00:02:23,433 --> 00:02:25,800
so we fire them up, literally

37
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:30,433
And, once they heat up enough, they will start spinning

38
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,233
Since we were not getting enough water

39
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:36,933
we have also upgraded our pump to use a steam engine

40
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,500
Going back to our 4-engine setup

41
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:46,433
we use some bevel gears and some shaft junctions to merge their power into a single output

42
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:51,200
This will sum the strength of the motors, thus summing the torque

43
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,466
while the speed will be kept the same

44
00:02:53,966 --> 00:03:00,733
This will bring us to a total of 65 kilowatts with a torque of 128 newton meters

45
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:02,466
While we have enough power

46
00:03:02,466 --> 00:03:06,466
we still lack both torque and strength for using the extractor

47
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:10,333
Thus we add a 4 to 1 gearbox to reach the minimum torque

48
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:14,333
required for stage 1 and 4 of the extracting process

49
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:17,600
However, when we place the extractor

50
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:21,000
we notice that we still haven't reached the required power

51
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:24,733
And that is because our stone gears are getting damaged

52
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:28,233
The more damage they take, the more power we lose

53
00:03:28,233 --> 00:03:31,133
To fix that, we are going to need lubricant

54
00:03:31,466 --> 00:03:35,966
And we should have not used stone gears without lubricant to begin with

55
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:42,200
Anyways, we quickly make a setup that will extract lubricant from canola seeds

56
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:48,366
And, using a lubricant hose, we move that all the way to our stone gearbox

57
00:03:49,166 --> 00:03:53,700
While that will prevent the gears from getting further damaged, it will not repair them

58
00:03:53,933 --> 00:03:55,766
so we add some new gears

59
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,733
Now that we have recovered the lost power

60
00:03:58,733 --> 00:04:02,166
we can finally start testing out our extractor

61
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:06,400
We managed to completely pulverize our first ore

62
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:09,766
but we now lack the speed for the second processing stage

63
00:04:10,433 --> 00:04:15,166
So we swap our torque gearbox with a 16 to 1 speed gearbox

64
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:20,400
And we should have switched gear to speed mode before connecting it to the system

65
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:24,266
We do that again, this time with speed mode

66
00:04:24,266 --> 00:04:28,366
and we can see that we are now doing the second stage of the ore processing

67
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:33,200
Then we do the third stage in parallel, all at full speed mode

68
00:04:33,766 --> 00:04:36,866
Until we finally get stuck on the fourth stage

69
00:04:36,866 --> 00:04:40,366
which requires us to change gears back to torque mode

70
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:43,800
And, after a long and slow processing

71
00:04:44,133 --> 00:04:47,833
we managed to extract nine flakes out of a single ore

72
00:04:48,366 --> 00:04:53,200
Using a smeltery, we can turn these into more than 49 ingots

73
00:04:54,266 --> 00:04:56,266
Now, this looks nicely

74
00:04:56,533 --> 00:05:01,100
but we can't stay here and change gears every time manually with a pickaxe

75
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:04,200
so we shall slightly edit this system to be more automated

76
00:05:04,766 --> 00:05:09,400
To have an automatic gear shift system, we first need a multidirectional clutch

77
00:05:09,766 --> 00:05:13,633
which can change the output side based on redstone power level

78
00:05:13,966 --> 00:05:17,366
Once we correctly set up everything, we can have a system

79
00:05:17,366 --> 00:05:23,533
where, by toggling a lever, we choose between low speed high torque or high speed low torque

80
00:05:24,166 --> 00:05:29,400
However, we do not want to stand there toggling a lever, so we use a sequencer

81
00:05:29,866 --> 00:05:33,766
And here we can see our timed automatic gear shift in action

82
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,766
Finally, we add some more gears

83
00:05:36,766 --> 00:05:40,266
and set the timer in a funny way to see how the mechanism works

84
00:05:42,033 --> 00:05:45,833
Now that our ore facility is slowly working on its own

85
00:05:46,166 --> 00:05:51,233
we should probably do something for the lubricant production before we run out of canola seeds

86
00:05:52,266 --> 00:05:55,766
To do so, we are going to apply a fan to our farm

87
00:05:56,133 --> 00:06:01,133
Once we turn it on, it will blow so hard that it will get the seeds out of the plants

88
00:06:02,066 --> 00:06:04,700
And look how nice of a job it is doing

89
00:06:05,433 --> 00:06:09,233
That will only push all the seeds as dropped items on the ground

90
00:06:09,233 --> 00:06:13,700
We could collect these with a hopper, but an item vacuum will do a better job

91
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:18,566
Finally, we use Thermal Expansion's tubes to move the items

92
00:06:19,866 --> 00:06:24,300
Now that we have fully automated lubricant, we can look at what we can do next

93
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:28,066
possibly a better power source to speed up our extractor

94
00:06:28,266 --> 00:06:33,900
We could make a gasoline engine, but that's just as much power as our 4 steam engines

95
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:41,133
An AC redstone engine seems to require manual maintenance, so let's skip that one too

96
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:47,966
The performance engine makes as much power as 16 steam engines, but it requires fuels

97
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:52,500
And it still can't power the extractor without gear shifting

98
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:59,100
So, an interesting choice is a watermill, which makes a lot of torque but at low speed

99
00:06:59,766 --> 00:07:04,366
And it only eats lubricant, which we have automated in a renewable way

100
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:08,033
The only issue is that, to be crafted

101
00:07:08,033 --> 00:07:13,600
we need a metal that requires us to bring the blast furnace at 1000 degrees

102
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:17,566
Lava can only bring us to 600 degrees

103
00:07:17,566 --> 00:07:20,666
so let's try going above that with a friction heater

104
00:07:20,933 --> 00:07:26,533
And by hooking it up to 4 steam engines, it seems that we won't reach 800 degrees

105
00:07:26,866 --> 00:07:31,000
which is not even enough for a material required by the performance engine

106
00:07:31,433 --> 00:07:35,366
By looking at the wiki, we can see the formula for the temperature

107
00:07:35,366 --> 00:07:39,700
which is logarithmic, and that we should try to balance speed and torque

108
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:44,600
However, even if we balance the torque and speed of 4 steam engines

109
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,566
we still can't reach even 800 degrees

110
00:07:48,166 --> 00:07:50,066
If we added 4 more engines

111
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:55,100
we could get really close to the heat required for making the performance engines

112
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:57,066
a 9th one should make it

113
00:07:57,333 --> 00:08:03,166
So, we add one more engine and look for a place where we can take the power of 4 others

114
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:08,033
And, exactly when we finished the setup, something went wrong

115
00:08:08,466 --> 00:08:15,466
It looks like shaft junctions can't merge the power of more than 4 generators until we gain access to Bedrockium

116
00:08:15,966 --> 00:08:17,600
So we need another solution

117
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:21,800
And I think that, for this job, AC engines are perfect

118
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:27,666
And, by the way, we can use some of the leftover parts to power a furnace

119
00:08:27,666 --> 00:08:30,600
Now we can smelt items faster and for free

120
00:08:30,866 --> 00:08:34,100
We quickly swap the steam engines with AC motors

121
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:40,366
but, other than giving them alternated redstone signals, we also need a magnetized shaft

122
00:08:40,866 --> 00:08:42,800
which we make in a magnetizer

123
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,800
Once we get one of these in our inventory

124
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:50,333
we can see that the motors start spinning as soon as we get close to them

125
00:08:51,433 --> 00:08:58,200
And, once we drop in the shafts, we can finally get enough heat to even melt down spring steel

126
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Now we can craft the hydrokinetic engine

127
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:05,666
but we can't run it at full power due to its massive torque

128
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:08,800
To do that, we would need diamond gears

129
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:12,033
but these require more heat than we can reach at the moment

130
00:09:12,866 --> 00:09:17,433
And, even if we used a well-balanced 4 performance engine setup

131
00:09:17,433 --> 00:09:23,866
we would still only reach 1230 degrees, which is still not enough

132
00:09:24,466 --> 00:09:28,000
So, our next option is to make a microturbine

133
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:34,200
that burns jet fuel and works at 131,000 revolutions per minute

134
00:09:34,966 --> 00:09:38,166
Such speed can't be managed with steel gears

135
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:42,000
but we can make the tungsten alloy ones that can handle it

136
00:09:42,533 --> 00:09:48,300
But, there is still something we can't make for the microturbine, inductive ingots

137
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:51,133
For these, we need a pulse jet furnace

138
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,433
Since that machine too requires high speed

139
00:09:54,433 --> 00:09:59,700
we start off by making some tungsten alloy ingots for the new gearboxes

140
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:02,400
Once we finish off the new gears and furnace

141
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:05,766
we realize that speed is not enough to run this machine

142
00:10:06,266 --> 00:10:08,000
We also need jet fuel

143
00:10:08,866 --> 00:10:15,400
To get jet fuel we have to start all the way back from finding oil, which spawns in the deserts

144
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:20,600
We set up a pump and fill a bunch of tanks so that we can bring it back home

145
00:10:21,033 --> 00:10:23,733
We dry some of it to obtain tar sand

146
00:10:24,233 --> 00:10:27,533
and we refine the rest to produce some fuel

147
00:10:27,533 --> 00:10:32,366
which we use to power a combustion engine so that we can refine even more

148
00:10:32,866 --> 00:10:37,033
Once we have a decent amount, we bring it to a fuel enhancer

149
00:10:37,033 --> 00:10:42,400
where, with the help of some expensive materials, we can finally obtain jet fuel

150
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,400
Now that our jet furnace is ready

151
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:49,266
we can redirect the power from our blast furnace to the jet one

152
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:55,533
This furnace can smelt even steel armors, but we are going to use it for inductive ingots

153
00:10:56,066 --> 00:11:00,766
Now that we have these, we can redirect the power to the blast furnace

154
00:11:00,766 --> 00:11:07,266
where we use these new ingots to make the missing part of the microturbine, a high-temperature combustor

155
00:11:07,733 --> 00:11:12,800
We finish our turbine, take half of the jet fuel we made and power it on

156
00:11:13,266 --> 00:11:18,833
And it turns out that the turbine needs some time at high fuel consumption to speed up

157
00:11:19,266 --> 00:11:24,800
With half of the fuel we made so far, we barely made it reach 1/10 of its power

158
00:11:25,266 --> 00:11:28,666
We should probably automate the production of fuel ingredients

159
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:31,966
but we are trying to make this just a temporary setup

160
00:11:31,966 --> 00:11:36,533
so we gather some more ingredients and do one more batch of jet fuel

161
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,466
This time we made 2 buckets

162
00:11:39,466 --> 00:11:43,400
we give all of that to the turbine and wait for it to speed up

163
00:11:43,866 --> 00:11:47,366
And, once we managed to reach the working speed

164
00:11:47,366 --> 00:11:51,566
we realize one was not enough for the temperature required for diamond gears

165
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:57,933
To fix that, we would need a second turbine, but we also run out of fuel

166
00:11:58,133 --> 00:12:00,166
so let's try something else

167
00:12:00,666 --> 00:12:03,266
We shall try a hydrokinetic engine

168
00:12:03,733 --> 00:12:09,533
This machine will produce power at low speed but super high torque when water flows on it

169
00:12:10,033 --> 00:12:14,266
When the waterfall is just 4 meters high, the power is really low

170
00:12:14,266 --> 00:12:16,833
but if we make a high water dam

171
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:21,900
we can see that we can achieve a torque so high that even tungsten gears can't handle it

172
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:24,700
and that's why we needed the diamond ones

173
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:32,366
Now, we could try to find a waterfall height that produces a manageable power and a complex gear setup

174
00:12:32,366 --> 00:12:37,433
but I'd rather climb on a flying island to get some magical slime tree saplings

175
00:12:38,133 --> 00:12:41,200
Once we get our loot, we can head back home

176
00:12:41,733 --> 00:12:47,366
where we can start working on a fresh batch of jet fuel and a second microturbine

177
00:12:48,233 --> 00:12:53,100
Once we have stocked up enough fuel, we bring it to the turbines and turn them on

178
00:12:53,566 --> 00:12:57,700
And we managed to reach the working speed almost when out of fuel

179
00:12:58,166 --> 00:13:02,066
Luckily they consume little amounts once they reach top speed

180
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:05,633
Since it took us so much to power this furnace

181
00:13:05,633 --> 00:13:09,100
we shall make enough diamond gears for the rest of the playthrough

182
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:13,866
I mean, let's just make as many as we can before we run out of fuel

183
00:13:14,566 --> 00:13:17,400
And I think we managed to make more than enough

184
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:21,300
hopefully we won't have to go find any more fuel materials

185
00:13:21,966 --> 00:13:24,933
Or maybe the fuel materials will find us

186
00:13:25,366 --> 00:13:30,300
I think they looked for us not to be turned into jet fuel but to take revenge

187
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:33,800
Moving on, we should probably turn on the hydro dam

188
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,766
but it looks like someone drank all of the water

189
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:40,100
And that's probably how the King Slime got so big

190
00:13:40,666 --> 00:13:43,700
Okay, we should not jump to conclusions

191
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:47,033
It was just too cold and the water froze

192
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:51,666
Now you can see how much power and strength this watermill makes

193
00:13:51,666 --> 00:13:55,433
But, fear not, diamond gears can manage that

194
00:13:56,066 --> 00:13:58,500
And now the output is more manageable

195
00:13:58,866 --> 00:14:00,400
But we don't have space

196
00:14:00,833 --> 00:14:05,800
So I think it is time to redo our whole base with this new power source

197
00:14:11,033 --> 00:14:16,100
Once we have done a nice cleaning, we shall start working on something inside the mountain

198
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:21,633
and that is a lubricant farm, since that's the only thing the watermill consumes

199
00:14:21,633 --> 00:14:27,500
However, it looks like working with such high powers on a single centrifuge is not efficient

200
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:31,133
and we could be using up more lubricant than we are producing

201
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:34,933
So, we shall step back and do a different kind of setup

202
00:14:34,966 --> 00:14:38,366
that also puts to good use the old stuff we salvaged

203
00:14:38,366 --> 00:14:44,500
And there we have it, 5 centrifuges and 5 grinders powered by the old steam engines

204
00:14:44,966 --> 00:14:50,666
Now that we have a lot of lubricant, we can go back and focus on our main power network

205
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:58,333
We shall bring the torque down to 256 newton meters at a higher speed, 8000 revolutions per minute

206
00:14:58,766 --> 00:15:03,233
Such power configuration can even be managed by stone shafts

207
00:15:03,433 --> 00:15:07,066
But, before getting to work, we shall close off the dam

208
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:12,000
Instead of using a clutch, we are going to remove the water from the mills

209
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,433
that way we stock up lubricant too

210
00:15:14,866 --> 00:15:18,300
Instead of splitting off the power to machines we don't need

211
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:25,066
we are going to use multidirectional clutches to choose which machine shall receive the full power of the hydro dam

212
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:27,900
And now it is time to do a run test

213
00:15:28,466 --> 00:15:34,566
For the moment, we can choose between directing the power into heating a blast furnace or a vanilla furnace

214
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:39,233
And, as you can see, only one at a time will get the power

215
00:15:39,766 --> 00:15:42,033
Next we add all of the other machines

216
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:46,366
and we even have a jet furnace which runs at 2 million RPM

217
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,266
And, when we shut down everything

218
00:15:49,666 --> 00:15:53,933
the stone cables will redirect the kinetic energy to our extractor

219
00:15:53,933 --> 00:15:57,166
which still can't run all the four stages at once

220
00:15:57,666 --> 00:15:59,700
And I think that's enough for today

221
00:16:00,166 --> 00:16:01,833
In the next episode

222
00:16:01,833 --> 00:16:07,033
we could try to see if we find a way of making so much power to break even the bedrock

223
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:08,366
Bye-bye

